window.docContents[14].resolve({"/The-p-adic-family-of-Eisenstein-series/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--The-p-adic-family-of-Eisenstein-series":{"contents":"We close Part I with a brief detour illustrating a second flavour of -adic\nvariation in number theory: the -adic variation of modular forms. Almost all\nthe work has already been done. In building the Kubota–Leopoldt -adic\n-function we constructed a pseudo-measure  on  interpolating\nthe values ; we will now see that these values are exactly the\nconstant terms of a family of Eisenstein series, and that the remaining Fourier\ncoefficients of that family are far easier to interpolate. Assembling the two\ngives a single power series — a -adic modular form — whose specialisations\nare honest modular forms.\n\nThroughout,  is a fixed prime, \nis the upper half-plane and .\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"An introduction to p-adic L-functions — Lean blueprint","header":"8. The p-adic family of Eisenstein series","id":"/The-p-adic-family-of-Eisenstein-series/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--The-p-adic-family-of-Eisenstein-series"}});